1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:05,249
Let's install Account Access, connect a shopping account, and ask our AI agent to

2
00:00:05,249 --> 00:00:09,870
find the best priced products. You'll see the setup once, then use the account

3
00:00:09,870 --> 00:00:12,180
through your normal agent conversation.

4
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:18,091
Start with Git, the u v package manager, and Codex or Claude Code installed

5
00:00:18,091 --> 00:00:23,009
and signed in. The guide below includes the installation links and every command you

6
00:00:23,009 --> 00:00:23,536
can copy.

7
00:00:25,117 --> 00:00:29,639
Download the repository, then open its folder with the change directory command.

8
00:00:29,639 --> 00:00:32,578
Run the next installation commands from this folder.

9
00:00:34,117 --> 00:00:36,654
Prepare Python and the required packages.

10
00:00:36,654 --> 00:00:40,367
Install Chromium for website access. Then build the package.

11
00:00:40,367 --> 00:00:43,275
Your first installation may take a few minutes.

12
00:00:44,783 --> 00:00:46,992
Install Account Access as a command.

13
00:00:46,992 --> 00:00:51,471
If the terminal cannot find it afterward, run u v tool update shell, then

14
00:00:51,471 --> 00:00:52,698
open a new terminal.

15
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:57,381
Initialize the account using its service connector.

16
00:00:57,381 --> 00:01:00,750
This walkthrough uses the included shopping connector.

17
00:01:00,750 --> 00:01:03,869
Install the skill for Codex, Claude Code, or both.

18
00:01:03,869 --> 00:01:06,364
Each agent gets its own access identity.

19
00:01:07,867 --> 00:01:10,642
Start the service and leave this terminal open.

20
00:01:10,642 --> 00:01:13,653
Account Access runs locally while your agent works.

21
00:01:13,653 --> 00:01:16,309
Now open a second terminal for account setup.

22
00:01:17,867 --> 00:01:20,489
Run account access setup in the second terminal.

23
00:01:20,489 --> 00:01:25,188
Your browser opens the account settings, where you connect the account and choose what

24
00:01:25,188 --> 00:01:26,117
the agent can do.

25
00:01:27,700 --> 00:01:30,055
Open the password form for your account.

26
00:01:30,055 --> 00:01:33,999
Enter your email or username and password, then click Save locally.

27
00:01:33,999 --> 00:01:38,061
Account Access can now sign in when you ask for an allowed operation.

28
00:01:39,617 --> 00:01:42,574
Select Codex or Claude and allow the catalog read.

29
00:01:42,574 --> 00:01:45,649
If you use both agents, grant that read to each one.

30
00:01:45,649 --> 00:01:50,498
This is a standing permission, so you don't repeat the approval for every request.

31
00:01:52,033 --> 00:01:55,408
In a fresh Codex chat, ask for the two cheapest products.

32
00:01:55,408 --> 00:01:59,080
The agent reads the permitted catalog and compares the prices.

33
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:03,402
It returns the onesie at seven dollars ninety nine, and the bike light at

34
00:02:03,402 --> 00:02:04,883
nine dollars ninety nine.

35
00:02:06,450 --> 00:02:09,235
You can use the same account from Claude Code.

36
00:02:09,235 --> 00:02:13,533
Ask for the backpack price. It returns twenty nine dollars ninety nine.

37
00:02:13,533 --> 00:02:18,134
The saved account session is reused, so you do not enter the password again.

38
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:25,321
That's the workflow: install Account Access, connect your account, grant access, and ask your

39
00:02:25,321 --> 00:02:28,162
agent to do the work. Keep the service running.

40
00:02:28,162 --> 00:02:32,937
If a website needs your approval later, complete that step in account setup and

41
00:02:32,937 --> 00:02:34,025
continue the task.
